Absolutely. Below is a **complete beginner-to-working-project implementation**. I’ll keep the first version practical and small enough that you can actually build it, then add the RAG/pgvector part.

The project will be:

> **AI PostgreSQL DBA Health Assistant for AWS RDS PostgreSQL 15.16**

It will collect PostgreSQL health information, send the findings to **Amazon Bedrock**, and display an AI-generated DBA analysis in **Streamlit**. Then we’ll add **pgvector + historical incidents** so it becomes a small RAG application.

AWS currently documents PostgreSQL 15.16 as a supported RDS version and lists `pgvector` among the supported extensions for PostgreSQL 15. ([AWS Documentation][1])

