# 22. One important DBA safety rule

**Do not allow the LLM to automatically execute SQL against your RDS database.**

Initially make the application:

```text
AI
 ↓
Recommendation
 ↓
DBA reviews
 ↓
DBA executes
```

Not:

```text
AI
 ↓
DELETE / TERMINATE / VACUUM FULL / ALTER
 ↓
Production
```

For example, the AI may recommend:

```sql
SELECT pg_terminate_backend(12345);
```

Your application should **never automatically execute that**.

The first version should be **read-only**.

Give the monitoring user only the permissions required for monitoring. This also follows the least-privilege approach recommended in AWS guidance. ([AWS Documentation][10])

